00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.720
Why do we build and test?

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.190
Well, build [? is ?]
a requirement.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.200
Our software won't
work until we turn it

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.240
into something that can run.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.950
Test is a choice.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:48.130
But it's a choice that
we're all making, right?

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.640
Well, let's talk about that.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.070
There is a wide body of
research talking about how

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.080
testing is really good.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.220
Testing makes your code better,
which makes your users happy,

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.500
which makes your
organization happy,

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.970
which makes us successful
as individuals.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.990
And when we add automation,
we can do testing at scale.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:10.080
We can grow our code base,
grow our organization,

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.710
and keep our software running
successfully, correctly.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.670
So look at the slide.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.970
It's all green.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:19.200
Whoops, meant to get the
laser here-- the green laser.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:19.950
It's all green.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.167
There's no red,
there's no pro/con.

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:23.250
We're all doing it, right?

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.690
We've totally
bought into testing,

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:32.760
and this is in our bones
